     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That is double the maximum labeled daily dose, which is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release (usually 2,000 mg/day in practice) and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A dose that high raises the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity, even with normal renal function.\n\nCould this be a typo or a mix-up? Some possibilities:\n- **850 mg three times daily** (2,550 mg/day, the maximum for immediate-release)\n- **1000 mg twice daily** (2,000 mg/day)\n- **500 mg three times daily** or **1700 mg total per day**, divided into doses\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want and I'll enter it right away. If you do want 1700 mg three times daily, please confirm that and I'll add a note documenting that you intended it. I'd still suggest checking with pharmacy first."
      }
